Asking for a key inside a fence that is not YAML reports the key as
missing rather than reporting the broken fence.

Frontmatter.parseFenced swallows the Yams failure into an empty
dictionary, so `get` finds nothing, and the command prints nothing and
exits 0. `md frontmatter --key title` therefore answers the same way
for a file whose fence will not parse as for a file whose fence simply
has no title.

The parse failure should be reported on stderr with a non-zero exit.
